|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_omega_

    If the expression 

    $$
    \Large \cos(\omega t)
    $$

    is to be dimensionally consistent,
    and if $t$ has units of seconds, then what units
    must $\omega$ have?

    |> Solution

        Since

        $$
        \cos : [1] \ra [1]
        $$

        or

        $$
        \cos : [\rad] \ra [1]
        $$

        rephrased (we have $[\rad] = [1]$, putting “radians” is a
        matter of “author's choice” semantic emphasis), $\omega$ must have units of

        __radians per second__

        or

        __per second__

        (equiv.) in order to cancel out the seconds in “$t$”.

        |> Image
            src=images/e6_bottom_radian_cloud.svg

